  m_text: 'The Pegasus constellation is defined by the Great Square, a massive four-star
    asterism that serves as a vital navigational landmark. In Greek mythology, this
    celestial stallion was the thunderbolt-carrier for Zeus, but today it is best
    known for the star Alpheratz, which physically links the horse''s wing to the
    constellation Andromeda. For stargazers, this giant "baseball diamond" in the
    sky acts as a cosmic window and the perfect starting point for exploring the
    surrounding constellations of the northern hemisphere.

'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
