      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Orion is defined by the Belt of Orion, a distinct line of three stars
    that serves as a vital navigational pointer in the winter sky. While it represents
    a legendary hunter, its primary importance to stargazers is the Orion Nebula,
    a massive stellar nursery visible to the naked eye within his sword. This region
    is anchored by the blue supergiant Rigel and the aging red supergiant Betelgeuse,
    providing a clear example of different stages in a star''s life cycle. For observers,
    the belt acts as a perfect celestial guide, leading the eye directly toward the
    bright star Sirius and the star clusters of Taurus.

'
