      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The Cygnus constellation is defined by the Northern Cross, a large and
    symmetrical asterism that serves as a reliable anchor for navigating the Milky
    Way. While it represents a celestial swan, its primary importance to stargazers
    is the star Deneb, which forms one corner of the Summer Triangle and is one of
    the most distant stars visible to the naked eye. For observers, the "head" of
    the swan features Albireo, a famous double star that reveals beautiful contrasting
    sapphire and gold colors when viewed through a telescope. This constellation
    acts as a perfect starting point for exploring the dense star clouds and deep-sky
    nebulae located along the galactic plane.

'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b9b90de0ca5051d438a676d0dd5ee5a7, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 1278191709768218732, guid: b9b90de0ca5051d438a676d0dd5ee5a7,
